; woods_crown.room - Copa da Orla (design 04 section 3.4; WORLD-35 step 2): the crown of a tree over woods_edge. From
; the hut roof (woods_edge row 4) a double jump rises 7 rows up through the hole (cols 11-14) onto the crown floor
; beside it (the guide's 8.5 rows with both jumps held); the base jump (4.5 rows) falls short. The hole drops back past
; the roof to the bench's floor. West, rows 17-20 join woods_deep's east trunk beside its row-19 branch: the double jump
; climbs from the bench to the canopy route, and a walk from the deep woods' branches drops back to the bench. East of
; the hole, the trunk top (cols 17-18, row 15) is 6 rows over the floor and the branch over the hole (cols 10-15, row 9)
; 6 over the trunk: the cache needs the double jump. User, 2026-10-14: "Woods crown later, falls head with MEM-10
; (Recommended)".

